  "caseId": "case19",
  "description": "The one non-zero CSUTLDTC outcome both call sites DELIBERATELY TOLERATE. 14 October 1582 is the day before the Lillian epoch, so CSUTLDTC reports severity '0003' with message number '2513' (FC-UNSUPP-RANGE). The guard at :396-406 is a NOT = test on the message number, so this outcome falls through with no rejection and no message, at :392 and again at :412 - and the range is then submitted. Both dates are the same day on purpose: the tolerance has to hold at both call sites, and a translation that tolerated it at one would pass a case that exercised only the other. All seventeen records carry 1582-10-14 in records 11, 12 and 15. Expected values are STATICALLY DERIVED by reading app/cbl/CORPT00C.cbl, its copybooks, app/bms/CORPT00.bms and app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD - never captured from a COBOL run, which is impossible in this environment (risk R-A). Java has no transient data queue, so EXEC CICS WRITEQ TD QUEUE('JOBS') at :517 is reproduced through an explicit job-submission port; the eighty-byte content is identical and the dataset key JOBS names the TDQUEUE(JOBS) that app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD:499-505 defines as RECORDSIZE(80) RECORDFORMAT(FIXED) BLOCKFORMAT(UNBLOCKED) DISPOSITION(MOD).",
